{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>When she is a widow or divorcée.</b> From a Levite or from an Israelite." "<b>A widow or divorcée.</b> Let it say 'divorcée' and not say 'widow' — and I would say: now a divorcée, who is forbidden to an ordinary priest, returns; a widow, who is permitted to an ordinary priest — is it not logical that she should return? But then I might say: a divorcée who has no seed returns, but a widow — whether she has seed or has no seed — returns. Scripture says: <b>a widow</b> and <b>seed she has not</b>. Or, had it said 'widow' and not said 'divorcée,' I would say: a widow who has no seed returns, but a divorcée — whether she has seed or has no seed — does not return. Scripture says: <b>a divorcée</b> and <b>seed she has not</b>. 'Widow' — to be stringent upon her; 'divorcée' — to be lenient upon her." "<b>And she returns to her father's house.</b> Excluding a woman awaiting levirate marriage (שומרת יבם)." "<b>As in her youth.</b> Excluding a pregnant woman."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:20.816369843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}